The week before Thanksgiving is when every calendar fills up at once: a half day here, a day off there, an extra practice, a school concert.

FamGenie puts it all in one plan for each kid. Add their weekly activities, paste the school or team calendar link (most offer one under "Subscribe" or "Add to calendar"), or connect Google Calendar. Then the Today view shows where everyone should be.

Free to start. {link}

Wednesday, 4:30. One kid at swim across town, the other at a rehearsal on the opposite side. Who's driving?

FamGenie looks at your kids' schedules and flags when two activities overlap in different places, so you sort out the carpool on Sunday night instead of in the car.

{link}

Holiday weeks mean new places and new times, and that's when a pickup gets missed.

With late alerts on, FamGenie texts you once if a child hasn't confirmed 10 minutes after something on their schedule starts. Kids confirm with a tap or a quick reply, so you only hear about it when there's something to check. One text, not a stream of pings.

{link}
